WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.640
Third-party dependencies are part of the application risk surface.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.260
Teams need visibility into which packages, frameworks, images,

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.040
and services are used and where they are deployed.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:16.060
Unsupported software becomes difficult to defend because fixes may no longer be available.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.720
End-of-life frameworks, runtimes, plugins,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.940
and operating systems should be replaced or isolated according to risk.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.320
Supply chain risk includes vulnerable packages, malicious updates,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.740
compromised build tools, and untrusted images.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:37.640
SaaS teams should govern package sources and build processes as part of system operations.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.420
Dependency tracking supports timely response when new vulnerabilities are announced.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.760
Remediation decisions should consider exploitability, exposure, compensating controls,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.060
and customer impact. Maintain software inventory and ownership.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.000
Use patch management and dependency scanning.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.260
Prioritize remediation based on risk and exposure.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:04.560
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC7.1 - Vulnerability management;

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.580
CC8.1 - Change management.
